{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Sha'ban}}, {{l|en|Shaaban}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ar|شَعْبَان|notext=1}}, from {{m|ar|شَعَبَ||to scatter, to disperse}}.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The eighth [[month]] of the [[Islamic calendar]].
#* '''1958-1994''', {{w|Hamilton Gibb}} & CF Beckingham, in ''The Travels of Ibn Battutah'', Folio Society 2012, p. 19:
#*: They go out also to spend the night there on the night if mid-'''Sha'ban''', and the market people take out all kinds of eatables.

